  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>The given limiting form is the indeterminate form&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Thus, using&nbsp;Newton-Leibnitz&nbsp;Rule (differentiation under integral sign)&nbsp;and L&#39; Hospital Rule, we get,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>",
